1
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:16,560
Hello everybody, welcome back to IELTS Intermediate Speaking Course by PREP.

2
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:23,780
Speaking part 3 can be a bit challenging because the questions are more complex, abstract, and academic.

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,320
They require us to have certain background knowledge and ideas about different

4
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:32,400
topics and know how to organize our answers coherently.

5
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:37,280
Therefore, in today's lesson, I will guide you through a very effective

6
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,500
technique for brainstorming ideas in Speaking part 3.

7
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:47,620
The AEE technique, which stands for Answer, directly answer what the question is asking.

8
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:51,140
Explanation, provide an explanation for the answer.

9
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:55,160
And an example, give an example to support the answer.

10
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:59,660
Let's use the AEE technique to brainstorm ideas for the question.

11
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:03,300
Is money always the most important thing when choosing a job?

12
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:16,460
Have you finished?

13
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,840
Let's see how I brainstorm ideas for this question.

14
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:22,420
First, I answer the question directly.

15
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,160
Money is the most important factor.

16
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:29,600
However, if we only give such a short answer, it won't be

17
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:33,660
convincing and may affect the fluency and coherence score in your answer.

18
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:38,340
In addition, short answers don't allow us to use very grammar structures

19
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:45,280
and vocabulary, which can affect the lexical resource and grammatical range and accuracy scores, right?

20
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:48,440
So I'm going to add an explanation to my answer.

21
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:51,640
It ensures a comfortable and happy life.

22
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:59,100
Next, to use more vocabulary and make my answer more persuasive, I will provide an example as well.

23
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:05,700
It helps fulfill essential personal needs, such as housing, medical expenses, and nourishment.

24
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:09,620
Now, do you understand the AEE technique better?

25
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:12,780
Let's continue with the same question.

26
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,680
Is money always the most important thing when choosing a job?

27
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:22,660
I'll give you a different viewpoint using the AEE technique, but in a more advanced way.

28
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:23,140
Ready?

29
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:25,100
A. Answer.

30
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:29,680
Money is important, but for the career options that already offer a

31
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:33,420
satisfactory income, other factors should carry equal weight.

32
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:36,280
Then, I'm going to give an explanation.

33
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:41,340
Money is vital to meet essential personal needs, but I have another

34
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:44,730
explanation to reinforce my answer, so here's the second one.

35
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:48,920
A large paycheck can never compensate for an unfulfilling job.

36
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:51,280
Now, I'll give an example.

37
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:56,320
In Japan, many people might earn a high salary, but still feel unhappy.

38
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:59,820
From these two ways of answering, we can see that we don't

39
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:06,980
have to follow the exact order, from answer to explanation, then example, so feel free to use them in any order.

40
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:12,380
It's just a guide for us to brainstorm ideas and give us more detailed and convincing answers.

41
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:17,100
Now, let's try brainstorming another question related to career choice.

42
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:21,240
Which jobs would you say are the most respected in your country?

43
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:26,880
I'll give you 20 seconds to brainstorm ideas for this question, using the AEE technique.

44
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,620
20 seconds, starting now.

45
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:53,490
Have you finished?

46
00:03:54,170 --> 00:03:55,190
Here is my answer.

47
00:03:56,090 --> 00:03:57,750
A, answer, doctor.

48
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:05,310
E1, explanation, requires extensive education, training, professional capacity.

49
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:10,810
Example one, it takes six years to complete a medical degree and

50
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:13,970
two to four years of internship to become a general practitioner.

51
00:04:14,870 --> 00:04:18,890
Explanation two, play an important role in safeguarding public health.

52
00:04:18,890 --> 00:04:25,090
Example two, in the COVID-19 pandemic, many capable doctors have successfully

53
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:28,230
identified the symptoms, enabling timely treatment.

54
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:32,170
We should also note that the AEE technique is not the only

55
00:04:32,170 --> 00:04:36,010
way to brainstorm ideas for speaking part three questions, but it is

56
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:39,190
a highly effective technique that helps us stay on track.

57
00:04:39,830 --> 00:04:42,790
With this approach, you only need to write down the main ideas

58
00:04:42,790 --> 00:04:45,610
to help structure your thoughts and save you time.

59
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:50,790
All right, now we are well prepared to enter the IELTS speaking exam room.

60
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:51,850
Let's go.

61
00:04:56,590 --> 00:05:02,130
Now let's apply the AEE technique to some other questions in IELTS speaking part 3.

62
00:05:02,850 --> 00:05:06,130
I really encourage you to come up with your own ideas using

63
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:10,510
the AEE technique, just like you are in the exam room, without any help.

64
00:05:11,150 --> 00:05:17,050
However, if any question seems too difficult, you can answer by using my suggestions first.

65
00:05:17,670 --> 00:05:22,110
Then pause the video and think of your own ideas to give a complete answer.

66
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:23,290
Are you ready?

67
00:05:23,950 --> 00:05:26,450
If you're not ready yet, you can pause this video for a

68
00:05:26,450 --> 00:05:27,210
while to prepare.

69
00:05:27,850 --> 00:05:31,470
But remember, in the real exam, you won't have time to prepare.

70
00:05:32,030 --> 00:05:34,270
How do people spend their leisure time in your country?

71
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:36,630
I'll give you 10 seconds to brainstorm.

72
00:05:37,330 --> 00:05:38,610
10 seconds starts now.

73
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:52,520
Finished?

74
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:54,120
Here's my outline.

75
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:57,840
In our country, people like indoor activities.

76
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:04,220
Because they're inexpensive, not physically demanding, and can suit any personality and preference.

77
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:11,620
For example, there are various free genres of books and types of games available for people to enjoy at home.

78
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:17,020
The second question is, is it important for people to have time for leisure activities?

79
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:20,180
You have 10 seconds to brainstorm your ideas.

80
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:22,700
10 seconds starts now.

81
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:36,550
Finished?

82
00:06:37,330 --> 00:06:38,370
Here's my outline.

83
00:06:39,930 --> 00:06:44,190
Firstly, I answer, yes, it is important.

84
00:06:45,090 --> 00:06:52,410
Then I provide the first explanation, which is having time for leisure activities allows me to unwind.

85
00:06:53,170 --> 00:06:58,890
Next, I continue to explain that leisure activities also help facilitate personal growth.

86
00:06:59,710 --> 00:07:06,790
Finally, I provide an example to support the second explanation, which is how reading books can expand one's knowledge.

87
00:07:07,430 --> 00:07:08,530
Good job, everyone.

88
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:10,470
Let's move on to the last question.

89
00:07:11,230 --> 00:07:15,390
What types of leisure activities may become more popular in the future?

90
00:07:16,050 --> 00:07:18,770
You have 10 seconds to brainstorm your ideas.

91
00:07:19,430 --> 00:07:21,470
10 seconds starting now.

92
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:34,760
Finished?

93
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,480
Here's my outline.

94
00:07:39,370 --> 00:07:44,990
First, I provide an answer that outdoor pastimes may become more popular in the future.

95
00:07:45,470 --> 00:07:50,590
Then I provide the first explanation, people becoming more health conscious,

96
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:55,810
leading to a growing demand for outdoor activities that promotes physical fitness.

97
00:07:56,770 --> 00:08:03,590
Then I provide an example to support this explanation, such as activities like jogging and hiking.

98
00:08:04,430 --> 00:08:09,890
Finally, I provide another explanation to further clarify the answer, which is

99
00:08:09,890 --> 00:08:14,670
that outdoor activities may become popular due to the stress of modern desk jobs.

100
00:08:19,510 --> 00:08:21,950
Do you remember what AEE stands for?

101
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:27,310
We've also applied all the knowledge learned today in the IELTS Speaking Part 3 test.

102
00:08:28,070 --> 00:08:31,130
Don't forget to review this lesson and finish all the exercises.

103
00:08:31,990 --> 00:08:32,929
Till next time, everybody.

104
00:08:33,590 --> 00:08:33,970
Bye-bye.

